WEBVTT

1
00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:44.968
Mutants. Since the discovery
of their existence ...

2
00:00:45.052 --> 00:00:47.053
they have been
regarded with fear ...

3
00:00:47.138 --> 00:00:50.223
suspicion, often hatred.

4
00:00:50.308 --> 00:00:52.559
Across the planet, debate rages.

5
00:00:52.643 --> 00:00:56.062
Are mutants the next link
in the evolutionary chain ...

6
00:00:56.147 --> 00:00:58.565
or simply a new species
of humanity ...

7
00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:01.735
fighting for their share
of the world?

8
00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:04.821
Either way,
it is an historical fact:

9
00:01:04.906 --> 00:01:09.409
Sharing the world
has never been humanity's
defining attribute.

10
00:01:51.285 --> 00:01:53.703
"We are not enemies, but friends.

11
00:01:53.788 --> 00:01:55.705
"We must not be enemies.

12
00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.707
"Though passion
may have strained ...

13
00:01:57.792 --> 00:02:01.044
it must not break the bonds
of our affection."

14
00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:06.258
Lincoln said that
in his first inaugural address
as our nation's 16th president.

15
00:02:06.342 --> 00:02:08.843
It's one of my favorites.

16
00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.012
So, if you'll please
have your tickets ready ...

17
00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.098
we can begin the tour.

18
00:02:19.814 --> 00:02:21.815
Jackie, could you clear
my schedule this evening?

19
00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.818
I wanna have dinner
with my son.
Yes, Mr. President.

20
00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.515
Excuse me, sir.
Are you lost?

21
00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:07.861
Perimeter breach
at visitor's checkpoint.

22
00:03:11.407 --> 00:03:13.992
Multiple subjects.

23
00:03:14.076 --> 00:03:18.872
Mr. President, security breach.
Jackie, leave. Let's get him
out to the car.

24
00:03:20.916 --> 00:03:22.626
Exit's not clear. We don't 
know how many there are.

25
00:03:22.752 --> 00:03:24.711
Post five. Secure.

26
00:03:34.096 --> 00:03:36.514
- There's something in the corridor.
- To the shelter.

27
00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:38.767
Negative! Not clear!

28
00:03:43.939 --> 00:03:47.442
- It's outside the oval office.
- Lock this place down!

29
00:04:04.502 --> 00:04:06.753
- Don't shoot!
- There!

30
00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.279
My God.

31
00:07:12.982 --> 00:07:16.651
Neanderthals. We once believed
that they were wiped out ...

32
00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:20.321
by years of conflict
with a much more advanced
branch of humanity ...

33
00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:22.323
called Cro-Magnon man.

34
00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.325
But recent research
into our own DNA ...

35
00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:28.079
suggests that these two species
may have interbred ...

36
00:07:28.163 --> 00:07:30.915
evolving into modern humans.

37
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.917
- In other words, into what?
- Us.

38
00:07:33.002 --> 00:07:35.962
Us. Right.

39
00:07:36.046 --> 00:07:38.923
Artie, not here.

40
00:07:45.347 --> 00:07:47.348
Come on.
Pay attention.

41
00:08:02.364 --> 00:08:04.365
Makes me insane
when she does this.

42
00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:08.161
What are you looking at, you sick --

43
00:08:08.245 --> 00:08:10.580
Busted my lip.

44
00:08:10.664 --> 00:08:12.624
- I have cancer.
- To the shelter!

45
00:08:12.708 --> 00:08:14.542
- No!
- Hi.

46
00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:17.503
They're gonna kill --

47
00:08:17.588 --> 00:08:20.048
What's wrong with this?
It doesn't work.

48
00:08:24.678 --> 00:08:26.638
Jean? You okay?
Yeah.

49
00:08:26.722 --> 00:08:29.390
Yeah, I'm fine.

50
00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:32.352
It's just, uh --
just a headache.

51
00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:36.731
It's not just a headache,
is it?

52
00:08:36.815 --> 00:08:39.734
Listen,
I -- I wasn't really
sure how to say this ...

53
00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.695
but ever since Liberty Island,
you've been --
Scott.

54
00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.739
You've been different.

55
00:08:44.823 --> 00:08:46.699
My telepathy's been off lately.

56
00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:50.203
I can't seem to focus.
I can hear everything.
It's not just your telepathy.

57
00:08:50.287 --> 00:08:54.165
A month ago, you had to concentrate
just to levitate a book
or a chair across the room.

58
00:08:54.249 --> 00:08:57.043
Now, when you have a nightmare,
the entire bedroom shakes.

59
00:09:00.047 --> 00:09:02.256
My dreams are getting worse.

60
00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:04.425
Scott.

61
00:09:06.387 --> 00:09:09.055
I keep feeling something terrible
is about to happen.

62
00:09:14.979 --> 00:09:18.106
I would never let anything
happen to you.

63
00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.067
Hey. Have you guys
seen Bobby and Rogue?

64
00:09:22.403 --> 00:09:24.904
Something's happening
in the food court.

65
00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.490
My brother asked you
a simple question.
Why are you being such a dick?

66
00:09:27.574 --> 00:09:29.575
Yeah, why are you
being such a dick?

67
00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:33.329
Because I can.

68
00:09:33.414 --> 00:09:35.415
Can I have a light?

69
00:09:37.251 --> 00:09:39.544
Hmm.

70
00:09:39.628 --> 00:09:41.671
- Sorry. I can't help you out, pal.
- John, knock it off.

71
00:09:41.755 --> 00:09:44.132
Why don't
you stop showing off?

72
00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:47.343
For her? I can't help it if your
girlfriend's getting excited.

73
00:09:47.428 --> 00:09:50.221
- I don't think
she's getting excited.
- Trying to have a good time.

74
00:09:50.305 --> 00:09:52.890
I think you're the only one
having a good time.

75
00:09:52.975 --> 00:09:55.810
Hey!

76
00:09:55.936 --> 00:09:58.771
That's real cute, man.
What are you gonna do?

77
00:10:01.358 --> 00:10:03.484
Suddenly,
you're not so tough.

78
00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:39.479
Hello? Honey, can you hear me?

79
00:10:48.155 --> 00:10:51.032
Bobby, what did you do?

80
00:10:51.158 --> 00:10:53.534
- I didn't do this.
- No.

81
00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:55.953
I did.

82
00:11:04.004 --> 00:11:08.049
And the next time you
feel like showing off, don't.

83
00:11:10.636 --> 00:11:15.598
Breaking news. We're coming
to you live from Washington ...

84
00:11:15.682 --> 00:11:18.476
where there's been
an attack in the Oval Office
of the White House.

85
00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.020
Details are still coming in,
but we have been informed ...

86
00:11:21.105 --> 00:11:24.023
that the president
and vice-president
were not harmed.

87
00:11:24.108 --> 00:11:26.692
Sources say the attack
involved one or more mutants.

88
00:11:26.777 --> 00:11:28.820
I think it's time 
to leave, Professor.

89
00:11:28.946 --> 00:11:31.656
- Authorities have closed off --
- I think you're right.

90
00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:38.204
Yearrgh! Unh!

91
00:11:42.042 --> 00:11:44.710
My opinion?
Magneto's behind this.

92
00:11:44.795 --> 00:11:46.712
No. I don't
think so, Scott.

93
00:11:46.797 --> 00:11:49.757
While Eric is capable
of organizing something
like this from prison ...

94
00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:51.759
for him
it would be irrational.

95
00:11:51.844 --> 00:11:53.761
It would only hurt his goal
of mutant prosperity.

96
00:11:53.887 --> 00:11:56.305
You mean superiority.
You're right.

97
00:11:56.390 --> 00:12:00.059
- If Eric had his way-
- Of course, you know how
the government will respond.

98
00:12:00.144 --> 00:12:02.311
They'll reintroduce
the Registration Act.

99
00:12:02.396 --> 00:12:06.566
Or worse. The president could
declare a state of emergency.

100
00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:09.152
Place every mutant
in the country under arrest.

101
00:12:09.236 --> 00:12:11.320
Do you think the assassin
was working alone?

102
00:12:11.405 --> 00:12:14.824
Well, we'll only know that
if we find him before
the authorities do.

103
00:12:14.908 --> 00:12:17.076
I've been trying to
track him using Cerebro ...

104
00:12:17.161 --> 00:12:21.664
but his movements
are inexplicably erratic.

105
00:12:21.748 --> 00:12:24.292
When I have
more exact coordinates ...

106
00:12:24.376 --> 00:12:27.461
Storm, Jean,
I'll need you to take the jet
and try and pick him up.

107
00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:32.842
It was close, wasn't it?

108
00:12:32.926 --> 00:12:35.803
Closer than anyone's admitted.

109
00:12:35.929 --> 00:12:38.514
What do you need,
William?
Just your authorization ...

110
00:12:38.599 --> 00:12:40.892
for a special operation.

111
00:12:41.935 --> 00:12:44.854
Uh, no, thank you,
Mr. President.

112
00:12:44.938 --> 00:12:47.690
And somehow I thought
you were here to talk
about school reform.

113
00:12:47.774 --> 00:12:50.067
Funny you should say that,
Mr. President.

114
00:12:50.194 --> 00:12:53.654
Senator.
Mr. President.

115
00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:57.366
- Thank you for having me.
- Senator Kelly, this is Colonel William Stryker.

116
00:12:57.451 --> 00:13:01.162
- How do you do?
- His department has been dealing
with the mutant phenomenon ...

117
00:13:01.246 --> 00:13:03.706
since before my time.

118
00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:06.959
As I recall,
you were a staunch supporter of
the Registration Act, Senator.

119
00:13:07.044 --> 00:13:10.296
It seems your ideas
on the mutant problem
have changed recently.

120
00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.548
For the best,
I hope.

121
00:13:12.633 --> 00:13:15.551
So, what are you proposing,
Mr. Stryker?

122
00:13:15.636 --> 00:13:17.929
Uh, may I,
Mr. President?

123
00:13:30.943 --> 00:13:34.528
We've managed to gather evidence
of a mutant training facility ...

124
00:13:34.613 --> 00:13:38.032
in the Salem region
of upstate New York.

125
00:13:38.116 --> 00:13:40.076
Where did you
get this information?

126
00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.745
Interrogation of one of
the mutant terrorists ...

127
00:13:42.829 --> 00:13:44.872
from the Liberty Island
incident.

128
00:13:44.957 --> 00:13:47.333
Eric? Eric Lehnsherr?

129
00:13:47.459 --> 00:13:50.586
- You have access to him?
- Magneto. Yes.

130
00:13:50.671 --> 00:13:53.839
We developed the technology
that built his plastic prison.

131
00:13:58.136 --> 00:14:01.722
- This facility is a school.
- Sure it is.

132
00:14:05.769 --> 00:14:07.687
What the hell is that?
A jet.

133
00:14:07.771 --> 00:14:10.898
- What kind of jet?
- We don't know ...

134
00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:15.569
but it comes up
out of the basketball court.

135
00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:24.954
If we'd been allowed to do our jobs,
Mr. President, before this incident --

136
00:14:25.038 --> 00:14:27.373
All right. Listen.

137
00:14:30.377 --> 00:14:33.671
William, you enter,
you detain, you question ...

138
00:14:33.755 --> 00:14:36.007
but the last thing
we need to see ...

139
00:14:36.091 --> 00:14:39.010
is the body of a mutant kid
on the 6:00 news.

140
00:14:47.602 --> 00:14:49.729
Mr. Stryker.
Senator Kelly.

141
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.983
This is Yuriko,
my personal assistant.

142
00:14:54.109 --> 00:14:57.028
Quite a handshake.
What can I do for you?

143
00:14:57.112 --> 00:15:00.865
Uh, Eric Lehnsherr's prison.
I'd like to arrange a visit
if possible.

144
00:15:00.949 --> 00:15:02.992
It isn't a petting zoo,
Senator.

145
00:15:03.076 --> 00:15:04.994
In this conflict,
he is the enemy.

146
00:15:05.078 --> 00:15:08.331
You're just a spectator.
So why don't you sit
this one out, all right?

147
00:15:08.415 --> 00:15:12.835
Conflict? Mr. Stryker,
do you really want to turn this
into some kind of war?

148
00:15:17.674 --> 00:15:20.843
I was piloting black-ops
missions in the jungles
of North Vietnam ...

149
00:15:20.927 --> 00:15:24.180
while you were sucking
on your mama's tit
at Woodstock, Kelly.

150
00:15:24.264 --> 00:15:26.182
Don't lecture me
about war.

151
00:15:26.266 --> 00:15:28.434
This already is a war.

152
00:15:38.278 --> 00:15:41.947
You're dead. You're so dead.
You're dead.

153
00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:49.288
I -- I don't
wanna hurt you.

154
00:15:51.458 --> 00:15:53.376
I'm not afraid.

155
00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:56.420
Hey.

156
00:16:11.895 --> 00:16:14.146
Logan!
It's Logan.

157
00:16:15.565 --> 00:16:17.525
You miss me, kid?

158
00:16:17.651 --> 00:16:19.944
Not really.
Mm. How you doing?

159
00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:22.488
I'm okay.
How are you?
Who's this?

160
00:16:22.572 --> 00:16:25.825
Oh, this is Bobby.
He's my --
I'm her boyfriend.

161
00:16:25.909 --> 00:16:28.327
Call me Iceman.

162
00:16:31.123 --> 00:16:34.583
Right.
Boyfriend?

163
00:16:34.668 --> 00:16:37.002
So how do you guys-

164
00:16:37.087 --> 00:16:40.297
Well, we're still
working on that.

165
00:16:40.382 --> 00:16:43.342
Look who's come back.
Just in time.

166
00:16:43.427 --> 00:16:46.679
For what?
We need a baby-sitter.

167
00:16:46.805 --> 00:16:50.266
Baby-sitter?
Nice to see you again,
Logan.

168
00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:54.854
- Hi, Logan.
- Hi, Jean.

169
00:16:54.938 --> 00:16:58.607
Uh, I should go
and get the jet ready.

170
00:16:58.692 --> 00:17:01.193
Yeah, well,
it was good to meet you.

171
00:17:01.319 --> 00:17:03.362
Come on.
Let's go.
Bye, Logan.

172
00:17:03.447 --> 00:17:06.323
I'll see you later.
- Okay.

173
00:17:10.328 --> 00:17:12.538
Storm and I
are heading to Boston.

174
00:17:12.622 --> 00:17:14.540
We won't be gone long.

175
00:17:14.624 --> 00:17:17.877
The professor wants us
to track down a mutant
who attacked the president.

176
00:17:17.961 --> 00:17:19.879
So it was a mutant?

177
00:17:19.963 --> 00:17:21.964
You'll be here
when we get back-

178
00:17:22.048 --> 00:17:24.967
unless you plan
on running off again.

179
00:17:25.051 --> 00:17:29.054
Well, I can probably think of
a few reasons to stick around.

180
00:17:30.557 --> 00:17:33.017
Find what you were
looking for, Logan?

181
00:17:33.101 --> 00:17:35.060
More or less.

182
00:17:35.145 --> 00:17:37.855
I'll see you boys later.

183
00:17:37.939 --> 00:17:40.649
- Be safe, okay?
- You too.

184
00:17:40.734 --> 00:17:43.277
- Bye.
- See ya.

185
00:17:45.489 --> 00:17:48.073
Aren't you gonna
welcome me home?

186
00:17:49.326 --> 00:17:52.328
Your bike needs gas.

187
00:17:52.412 --> 00:17:54.580
Then fill her up.

188
00:18:14.226 --> 00:18:16.143
Mr. Laurio.

189
00:18:16.228 --> 00:18:18.145
How long
can we keep this up?

190
00:18:20.232 --> 00:18:22.441
How long is your sentence?

191
00:18:22.567 --> 00:18:25.986
Forever.
Not necessarily forever,
Mr. Lehnsherr.

192
00:18:26.071 --> 00:18:28.489
Just until
I've got all that I need.

193
00:18:28.573 --> 00:18:30.699
Mr. Stryker.
How kind of you to visit.

194
00:18:30.784 --> 00:18:36.497
Have you come back to make sure
the tax-payers' dollars
are keeping me comfortable?

195
00:18:39.376 --> 00:18:42.294
Ohh!

196
00:19:00.981 --> 00:19:04.024
Done. You can go.

197
00:19:06.319 --> 00:19:08.362
Now ...

198
00:19:11.157 --> 00:19:13.325
Mr. Lehnsherr ...

199
00:19:16.496 --> 00:19:18.956
I'd like to have one final talk ...

200
00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.709
about the house
that Xavier built ...

201
00:19:21.793 --> 00:19:24.878
and the machine
called Cerebro.

202
00:19:33.388 --> 00:19:36.932
Logan, my tolerance for your smoking
in the mansion notwithstanding ...

203
00:19:37.017 --> 00:19:40.811
continue smoking that in here
and you'll spend the rest of your days ...

204
00:19:40.895 --> 00:19:43.147
under the belief that
you're a six-year-old girl.

205
00:19:43.231 --> 00:19:47.276
- You'd do that?
- I'd have Jean braid your hair.

206
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.237
Welcome back.

207
00:20:00.248 --> 00:20:02.166
Ooh.

208
00:20:06.171 --> 00:20:10.424
You want me to leave?

209
00:20:10.508 --> 00:20:13.052
No. Just don't move.

210
00:20:19.434 --> 00:20:22.770
These lights represent
every living person on the planet.

211
00:20:26.608 --> 00:20:28.734
White lights are humans.

212
00:20:31.738 --> 00:20:34.156
And these
are the mutants.

213
00:20:36.618 --> 00:20:39.370
Through Cerebro,
I'm connected to them.

214
00:20:39.454 --> 00:20:41.622
And they to me.

215
00:20:44.125 --> 00:20:46.710
You see, Logan ...

216
00:20:46.795 --> 00:20:49.046
We're not as alone
as you think.

217
00:20:51.633 --> 00:20:53.801
I found the base
at Alkali Lake.

218
00:20:54.969 --> 00:20:56.887
There was
nothing there.

219
00:20:56.971 --> 00:21:01.725
The broken line represents
the path of the mutant
who attacked the president.

220
00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:05.562
I've been finding it difficult
to get a lock on him.

221
00:21:05.647 --> 00:21:09.024
Well, can't you just
concentrate harder?

222
00:21:09.109 --> 00:21:11.652
If I wanted to kill him, yes.

223
00:21:13.363 --> 00:21:16.281
There.

224
00:21:16.366 --> 00:21:18.909
Looks like he's finally 
stopped running.

225
00:21:34.467 --> 00:21:36.885
I need you to read 
my mind again.

226
00:21:38.805 --> 00:21:40.848
Logan ...

227
00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.940
I'm afraid the results
will be the same as before.

228
00:21:50.024 --> 00:21:54.403
- We had a deal.
- The mind is not a box that can
be simply unlocked and opened.

229
00:21:54.487 --> 00:21:58.615
- It's a beehive with a million
different compartments.
- Spare me the lecture.

230
00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:02.828
I have no doubt that your amnesia,
your adamantium skeleton, the claws ...

231
00:22:02.912 --> 00:22:04.830
are all somehow connected.

232
00:22:04.914 --> 00:22:06.832
But, Logan ...

233
00:22:06.916 --> 00:22:11.879
sometimes the mind needs to
discover things for itself.

234
00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:14.590
I promise you we'll
talk again when I return.

235
00:22:14.674 --> 00:22:19.845
Oh. If you will be kind enough
to watch over the children tonight ...

236
00:22:19.929 --> 00:22:22.598
Scott and I are going to
visit an old friend.

237
00:22:36.571 --> 00:22:40.282
I'm sending coordinates of where the 
mutant seems to have settled for now.

238
00:22:40.366 --> 00:22:43.035
Soon as you find him,
bring him back to the mansion.

239
00:22:43.119 --> 00:22:45.037
Let's hope
he cooperates.

240
00:22:45.121 --> 00:22:47.956
Yes. For his sake.
Good luck.

241
00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:57.067
Stryker, William.

242
00:25:43.466 --> 00:25:46.510
What are you doing in here?

243
00:25:46.594 --> 00:25:49.763
Estoy tirando la basura.

244
00:25:49.847 --> 00:25:51.932
Garbage.

245
00:26:39.939 --> 00:26:41.940
These are the coordinates.

246
00:27:00.501 --> 00:27:03.170
He's a teleporter.

247
00:27:03.254 --> 00:27:07.257
Must be why the professor
had trouble locking onto him.

248
00:27:07.341 --> 00:27:11.011
We're not here to hurt you!

249
00:27:12.138 --> 00:27:14.056
We just wanna talk!

250
00:27:19.395 --> 00:27:22.147
- Are you bored yet?
- Oh, yeah.

251
00:27:22.231 --> 00:27:24.649
Sure you don't wanna come down?

252
00:27:47.507 --> 00:27:50.842
- You have him?
- He's not going anywhere.

253
00:27:50.927 --> 00:27:53.220
Are you?

254
00:27:53.304 --> 00:27:55.639
Please don't kill me.
I didn't mean to harm anyone.

255
00:27:55.723 --> 00:27:58.183
Now why would people
have gotten that impression?

256
00:27:59.477 --> 00:28:03.522
What's your name?
Wagner. Kurt Wagner.

257
00:28:07.985 --> 00:28:10.278
There was so much shooting ...

258
00:28:10.363 --> 00:28:12.280
such fear ...

259
00:28:12.365 --> 00:28:14.366
and then
there was only pain.

260
00:28:17.120 --> 00:28:19.371
I could see it all happening ...

261
00:28:19.455 --> 00:28:21.957
but I couldn't stop myself.

262
00:28:22.041 --> 00:28:24.543
It was like a bad dream.

263
00:28:25.586 --> 00:28:28.380
Perhaps He is testing me.

264
00:28:31.342 --> 00:28:33.301
And before you were
in the White House ...

265
00:28:33.386 --> 00:28:35.303
what do you remember?

266
00:28:35.388 --> 00:28:38.348
Nothing. I was here.

267
00:28:41.352 --> 00:28:43.353
Jean.

268
00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:46.523
I'd rather get him
back to the professor.

269
00:28:46.607 --> 00:28:48.400
The professor?

270
00:28:53.489 --> 00:28:56.074
Did you do these yourself?

271
00:28:57.118 --> 00:28:59.119
Yes.

272
00:29:04.041 --> 00:29:06.376
And what about this?

273
00:29:26.731 --> 00:29:28.648
I need you to read 
my mind again.

274
00:29:28.733 --> 00:29:31.109
I'm afraid the results
will be the same as before.

275
00:29:31.235 --> 00:29:33.445
He'll be indestructible.
- His entire skeleton --

276
00:29:33.571 --> 00:29:38.950
Adamantium.
- Sometimes the mind needs 
to discover things for itself.

277
00:29:39.076 --> 00:29:42.871
Wolverine.

278
00:29:42.955 --> 00:29:45.582
No memory. 
He'll have no memory.

279
00:29:57.178 --> 00:29:59.638
A dozen tourists in the 'White 
House' during the attack ...

280
00:29:59.722 --> 00:30:01.640
are still being
held for questioning.

281
00:30:01.724 --> 00:30:05.101
Best tasting food.
A machine that's so darn easy --

282
00:30:07.855 --> 00:30:09.648
... president will address the nation --

283
00:30:15.112 --> 00:30:18.198
For the White House assassin,
following hundreds of --

284
00:30:18.282 --> 00:30:19.783
Can't sleep?

285
00:30:21.285 --> 00:30:24.621
- How can you tell?
- 'Cause you're awake.

286
00:30:24.705 --> 00:30:27.916
Right. How about you?

287
00:30:28.042 --> 00:30:30.210
I don't sleep.

288
00:30:36.175 --> 00:30:38.301
Hey.

289
00:30:38.386 --> 00:30:40.387
Doesn't anybody
sleep around here?

290
00:30:40.471 --> 00:30:42.472
Apparently not.

291
00:30:43.641 --> 00:30:47.310
Got any beer?
This is a school.

292
00:30:47.436 --> 00:30:49.312
So that's a "no"?
Yeah, that's a "no."

293
00:30:49.397 --> 00:30:51.314
Got anything other
than chocolate milk?

294
00:30:51.399 --> 00:30:54.526
There should be some soda
in that small cupboard.

295
00:31:08.749 --> 00:31:10.667
Thanks.
No problem.

296
00:31:19.427 --> 00:31:21.428
I'll take him from here.

297
00:31:22.763 --> 00:31:25.307
It's all right, Scott.

298
00:31:25.433 --> 00:31:27.934
Nice shades.
Thanks.

299
00:31:57.715 --> 00:32:00.842
Charles Xavier.
Have you come to rescue me?

300
00:32:00.926 --> 00:32:02.802
Sorry, Eric. Not today.

301
00:32:02.887 --> 00:32:05.764
To what do I owe
the pleasure?

302
00:32:08.434 --> 00:32:10.518
The assassination attempt
on the president-

303
00:32:10.644 --> 00:32:13.688
What do you
know about it?
Nothing.

304
00:32:13.773 --> 00:32:16.066
Only what I read
in the papers.

305
00:32:16.150 --> 00:32:19.778
You really shouldn't
have to ask, Charles.

306
00:32:19.862 --> 00:32:22.113
What's happened to you?

307
00:32:22.198 --> 00:32:25.700
I've had frequent visits
from William Stryker.

308
00:32:25.785 --> 00:32:28.620
You remember him,
don't you?

309
00:32:29.747 --> 00:32:32.040
William Stryker.

310
00:32:32.124 --> 00:32:36.419
His son, Jason,
was once a student
of yours, wasn't he?

311
00:32:36.504 --> 00:32:38.546
Yes. Years ago.

312
00:32:38.631 --> 00:32:42.384
Unfortunately,
I wasn't able to help him ...

313
00:32:42.468 --> 00:32:44.719
at least not in the way
that his father wanted.

314
00:32:44.804 --> 00:32:47.222
And now you think
that taking in the Wolverine ...

315
00:32:47.306 --> 00:32:50.934
will make up for your failure
with Strykef's son.

316
00:32:54.814 --> 00:32:58.149
How long you been here?
Couple years.

317
00:32:58.234 --> 00:33:01.403
And your parents just sent you off
to mutant school?

318
00:33:03.072 --> 00:33:07.200
Actually, my parents
think this is a prep school.

319
00:33:08.285 --> 00:33:10.370
Oh, I see.

320
00:33:10.496 --> 00:33:14.124
I suppose lots of prep schools
have their own dorms, campuses --
Jets.

321
00:33:16.544 --> 00:33:19.504
So you and Rogue,
huh?
Yeah.

322
00:33:19.588 --> 00:33:22.674
It's not what you think.
I'd like it to be, but it's just --

323
00:33:24.135 --> 00:33:26.344
It's just that it's not easy ...

324
00:33:26.429 --> 00:33:28.721
when you wanna be
closer to someone ...

325
00:33:30.182 --> 00:33:32.725
but you can't.

326
00:33:34.937 --> 00:33:37.147
You know, I've seen how
you look at Dr. Grey.

327
00:33:38.441 --> 00:33:42.026
Excuse me?
Nothing.

328
00:33:42.111 --> 00:33:44.654
You haven't told him
about his past, have you?

329
00:33:44.738 --> 00:33:46.948
I've put him on the path.

330
00:33:47.032 --> 00:33:49.617
Logan's mind is still fragile.

331
00:33:49.702 --> 00:33:51.703
Is it?

332
00:33:51.787 --> 00:33:55.373
Or are you afraid of losing
one of your precious X-Men ...

333
00:33:55.458 --> 00:33:57.542
old friend?

334
00:34:00.921 --> 00:34:03.047
Eric, what have you done?

335
00:34:05.009 --> 00:34:07.010
I'm sorry, Charles.

336
00:34:08.554 --> 00:34:10.722
I couldn't help it.

337
00:34:11.932 --> 00:34:13.850
What have you told Stryker?

338
00:34:16.145 --> 00:34:18.062
Everything.

339
00:34:23.694 --> 00:34:26.237
The war has begun.

340
00:34:31.243 --> 00:34:36.247
Scott!
You should've killed me
when you had the chance!

341
00:35:09.949 --> 00:35:11.991
But now and then ...

342
00:35:12.076 --> 00:35:14.035
every mother needs to get away.

343
00:35:14.119 --> 00:35:17.372
Without her,
the babies are helpless.

344
00:35:17.456 --> 00:35:21.834
Sensing danger,
the mother rat races home.

345
00:35:21.919 --> 00:35:25.296
The babies can't
even see the killer.

346
00:35:25.381 --> 00:35:28.424
And someone uninvited
is coming to dinner.

347
00:35:30.302 --> 00:35:32.887
She arrives too late
for one baby.

348
00:35:32.972 --> 00:35:35.932
The centipede was deadly.

349
00:35:38.060 --> 00:35:39.602
Hi.

350
00:35:56.245 --> 00:35:58.454
- What is it?
- Shh, shh.

351
00:36:33.449 --> 00:36:35.366
You picked
the wrong house, bub.

352
00:37:14.365 --> 00:37:16.240
You all right?

353
00:37:26.585 --> 00:37:27.543
Stay here.

354
00:37:37.137 --> 00:37:39.639
Come on!
Run!

355
00:38:05.124 --> 00:38:07.917
Move, move, move!

356
00:38:15.175 --> 00:38:17.051
This way.
Let's go. Come on!

357
00:38:23.267 --> 00:38:25.143
Go, go, go!

358
00:38:31.859 --> 00:38:34.652
Run!

359
00:38:34.778 --> 00:38:37.280
Run!
John! Hey.
Where's Rogue?

360
00:38:37.406 --> 00:38:40.074
I don't know.
I gotta find her.

361
00:38:40.159 --> 00:38:41.659
Hey!

362
00:38:42.911 --> 00:38:45.329
Come on!
Here. Take her.

363
00:38:45.414 --> 00:38:47.582
Hurry!

364
00:38:50.878 --> 00:38:53.504
Go on. Get in.
Let's go. Let's go.

365
00:38:53.589 --> 00:38:55.506
Come on.
Let's go! Come on!

366
00:38:58.343 --> 00:39:01.304
Hey. Take him.
He's stunned.

367
00:39:01.430 --> 00:39:03.389
I can help you.
Help them.

368
00:39:26.371 --> 00:39:28.289
Rogue!
Bobby!

369
00:39:28.373 --> 00:39:30.374
This way.

370
00:39:41.303 --> 00:39:44.430
Come on. Everybody,
follow me up here.

371
00:39:50.604 --> 00:39:53.356
Move! Move!
Go! Go!

372
00:40:01.031 --> 00:40:03.032
Come on.

373
00:40:16.755 --> 00:40:19.298
Let's go.

374
00:40:19.383 --> 00:40:22.260
Come on. This way.

375
00:40:27.933 --> 00:40:30.059
This is it.

376
00:40:31.270 --> 00:40:33.271
Logan!

377
00:40:33.355 --> 00:40:35.314
You wanna shoot me?
Shoot me!

378
00:40:35.399 --> 00:40:37.441
Don't shoot him!

379
00:40:37.526 --> 00:40:39.777
Not yet.

380
00:40:41.280 --> 00:40:43.322
Wolverine?

381
00:40:43.407 --> 00:40:45.783
Well, I must admit, this is
certainly the last place ...

382
00:40:45.868 --> 00:40:48.119
I'd expect to find you.

383
00:40:48.203 --> 00:40:50.955
How long has it been?
Fifteen years?

384
00:40:52.124 --> 00:40:54.458
You haven't
changed one bit.

385
00:40:54.543 --> 00:40:57.920
Me, on the other hand --

386
00:41:00.257 --> 00:41:02.258
Nature.

387
00:41:06.930 --> 00:41:09.765
Wait! Wait! You guys,
we gotta do something.
They're gonna kill him.

388
00:41:09.850 --> 00:41:12.310
- He can handle himself. Let's go.
- Bobby!

389
00:41:13.604 --> 00:41:15.855
Please.

390
00:41:15.939 --> 00:41:19.358
I didn't realize Xavier
was taking in animals --

391
00:41:19.443 --> 00:41:21.527
even animals
as unique as you.

392
00:41:21.612 --> 00:41:23.696
Who are you?

393
00:41:25.115 --> 00:41:27.700
Don't you remember?

394
00:41:42.341 --> 00:41:44.884
No! No!

395
00:41:47.846 --> 00:41:49.847
Logan, come on.
Let's go.

396
00:42:02.527 --> 00:42:06.614
Logan.
Go! I'll be fine.

397
00:42:06.698 --> 00:42:08.866
But we won't.

398
00:42:17.751 --> 00:42:19.418
Go. Keep going.

399
00:42:45.362 --> 00:42:47.530
All right. Get in. Get in!
I'm driving.

400
00:42:47.614 --> 00:42:50.282
Hey. Maybe next time.

401
00:42:52.744 --> 00:42:54.912
This is Cyclops's car.

402
00:42:55.956 --> 00:42:57.623
Oh, yeah?

403
00:43:15.809 --> 00:43:17.643
What the hell
was that back there?

404
00:43:19.604 --> 00:43:22.690
Stryker. His name is Stryker.

405
00:43:22.774 --> 00:43:24.817
Who is he?

406
00:43:24.901 --> 00:43:27.069
I can't remember.

407
00:43:27.154 --> 00:43:29.071
Zone one clear.

408
00:43:29.156 --> 00:43:31.449
Roger that.

409
00:43:36.288 --> 00:43:39.498
Here. This is yours.

410
00:43:49.134 --> 00:43:51.719
I don't like
uncomfortable silences.

411
00:43:51.803 --> 00:43:53.846
What are you doing?

412
00:43:59.770 --> 00:44:02.480
I don't think
that's the CD player.

413
00:44:05.233 --> 00:44:07.026
Whoa.

414
00:44:09.905 --> 00:44:11.864
Sit back.

415
00:44:11.948 --> 00:44:15.034
- Where we going?
- Storm and Jean are in Boston.
We'll head that way.

416
00:44:16.578 --> 00:44:19.330
- My parents live in Boston.
- Good.

417
00:44:35.430 --> 00:44:37.014
Sergeant?

418
00:44:37.099 --> 00:44:40.267
Most of the mutants escaped
through a series of tunnels
that weren't in our schematics.

419
00:44:40.352 --> 00:44:42.228
We have several in custody.

420
00:44:42.354 --> 00:44:44.188
How many?
Six, sir.

421
00:45:09.548 --> 00:45:12.716
Welcome, Professor.

422
00:45:34.072 --> 00:45:36.073
Take what we need, gentlemen.

423
00:45:38.034 --> 00:45:40.661
Look, I just think all this
anti-mutant protesting ...

424
00:45:40.745 --> 00:45:44.373
underscores
the genuine growing concern
among most Americans.

425
00:45:44.457 --> 00:45:46.375
I think
mutant registration --
But why stop there?

426
00:45:46.459 --> 00:45:49.920
Maybe it would be easier
to round up mutants
by the truckload.

427
00:45:50.005 --> 00:45:52.715
Or maybe you'd like
all-out war, Mr. Shaw.
Oh, please.

428
00:45:52.799 --> 00:45:55.342
Turn that shit off, Lou.

429
00:45:55.427 --> 00:45:57.928
Lot on your mind?

430
00:46:00.390 --> 00:46:03.893
Mr. Laurio?

431
00:46:05.562 --> 00:46:08.272
I'm Grace.

432
00:46:18.491 --> 00:46:20.451
You want another beer?

433
00:46:21.661 --> 00:46:23.746
Of course you do.

434
00:46:31.922 --> 00:46:35.007
You're really aggressive.
Yes, I am.

435
00:46:37.427 --> 00:46:40.512
Oh, I -- I've never hooked up
with a girl like you before.

436
00:46:40.597 --> 00:46:42.806
I know.

437
00:46:44.935 --> 00:46:47.102
It's, uh, kinda dirty in here,
don't you think?

438
00:46:47.187 --> 00:46:49.939
That's the idea. Velcro.

439
00:46:50.023 --> 00:46:53.150
Nice.
Bottom's up.

440
00:46:53.235 --> 00:46:55.444
I certainly hope so.

441
00:47:11.628 --> 00:47:13.545
Bottom's up.

442
00:47:33.566 --> 00:47:36.193
- William.
- Please, Xavier, don't get up.

443
00:47:38.446 --> 00:47:40.656
I call it the 
neural inhibitor.

444
00:47:40.740 --> 00:47:43.909
It keeps you outta here.

445
00:47:45.370 --> 00:47:47.288
What have you
done with Scott?

446
00:47:47.372 --> 00:47:51.417
Don't worry.
I'm just giving him
a little re-education.

447
00:47:51.501 --> 00:47:54.753
Of course, you know
all about that, don't you?

448
00:47:54.838 --> 00:47:56.880
William, you wanted me
to cure your son.

449
00:47:57.007 --> 00:47:59.508
But mutation
is not a disease.
You're lying!

450
00:48:01.094 --> 00:48:04.096
You were more frightened
of him than I was.

451
00:48:04.180 --> 00:48:08.475
You know,
just one year after Jason
returned from your school ...

452
00:48:08.560 --> 00:48:10.477
my wife --

453
00:48:10.562 --> 00:48:13.480
You see he resented us.

454
00:48:13.565 --> 00:48:16.066
He blamed us
for his condition.

455
00:48:16.151 --> 00:48:18.694
So he would
toy with our minds ...

456
00:48:18.778 --> 00:48:21.864
projecting visions
and scenarios into our brains.

457
00:48:21.948 --> 00:48:26.201
Well, my wife,
in the end --

458
00:48:26.286 --> 00:48:29.496
She took a power drill
to her left temple ...

459
00:48:29.581 --> 00:48:32.249
in an attempt
to bore the images out.

460
00:48:33.418 --> 00:48:36.920
My boy, the great illusionist.

461
00:48:43.678 --> 00:48:45.888
For someone
who hates mutants ...

462
00:48:45.972 --> 00:48:48.891
you certainly keep
some strange company.

463
00:48:48.975 --> 00:48:51.602
Oh, they serve
their purpose ...

464
00:48:51.686 --> 00:48:54.897
as long as
they can be controlled.

465
00:48:59.944 --> 00:49:02.529
You arranged the attack
on the president.

466
00:49:04.699 --> 00:49:07.159
You didn't even
have to read my mind.

467
00:49:10.372 --> 00:49:13.957
You know,
I've been working with mutants
as long as you have, Xavier ...

468
00:49:14.042 --> 00:49:16.126
but the most frustrating thing
I've learned ...

469
00:49:16.211 --> 00:49:19.088
is that nobody really knows
how many even exist ...

470
00:49:19.172 --> 00:49:21.298
or how to find them --

471
00:49:23.051 --> 00:49:25.594
except you.

472
00:49:25.678 --> 00:49:28.472
Unfortunately, this little potion
won't work on you, will it?

473
00:49:28.556 --> 00:49:30.808
You're much too powerful
for that.

474
00:49:30.892 --> 00:49:34.728
Instead, we'll go
right to the source.

475
00:49:36.314 --> 00:49:40.317
Allow me to introduce mutant 143.

476
00:49:41.903 --> 00:49:46.573
The fluid secreted by his brain
acts as a mind-controlling agent.

477
00:49:46.658 --> 00:49:49.785
But that's only
where it begins.

478
00:49:49.869 --> 00:49:51.829
Jason.

479
00:49:51.913 --> 00:49:55.457
Oh, my God, William.
This is your son.

480
00:49:55.583 --> 00:49:57.751
What have you
done to him?
No, Charles!

481
00:49:58.920 --> 00:50:01.338
My son is dead ...

482
00:50:01.423 --> 00:50:03.715
just like the rest of you.

483
00:50:27.782 --> 00:50:29.950
Mom? Dad? Ronny?

484
00:50:30.034 --> 00:50:34.288
Is anybody home?

485
00:50:34.372 --> 00:50:36.373
I'll try and find us
some clothes.

486
00:50:36.458 --> 00:50:39.585
Don't burn anything.

487
00:50:50.305 --> 00:50:54.808
Hey. I found some of
my mom's old clothes.

488
00:50:54.893 --> 00:50:57.060
I think they're from
before I was born.

489
00:51:00.064 --> 00:51:01.565
Groovy.

490
00:51:08.031 --> 00:51:13.660
Hello.

491
00:51:13.745 --> 00:51:16.538
Come on, Jean.
Where are you?

492
00:51:47.278 --> 00:51:50.572
These are
my grandmother's.

493
00:51:50.657 --> 00:51:52.950
Thanks.

494
00:51:54.953 --> 00:51:57.120
You won't hurt me.

495
00:52:06.422 --> 00:52:08.757
Wow.

496
00:52:17.850 --> 00:52:20.394
I'm -- I'm sorry.

497
00:52:22.855 --> 00:52:24.856
It's okay.

498
00:52:28.778 --> 00:52:30.779
Mmm.

499
00:52:52.594 --> 00:52:54.803
Hey, Ronny. Next time you --

500
00:52:56.097 --> 00:52:58.890
Who the hell are you?

501
00:52:59.017 --> 00:53:01.184
Uh --
Bobby.

502
00:53:01.269 --> 00:53:03.812
Honey, aren't you
supposed to be at school?

503
00:53:03.896 --> 00:53:09.693
- Bobby, who is this guy?
- Uh, this is Professor Logan.

504
00:53:16.242 --> 00:53:18.368
There's something 
I need to tell you.

505
00:53:38.389 --> 00:53:41.266
You're clear.

506
00:53:57.116 --> 00:53:59.242
Have a nice sleep, Lehnsherr?

507
00:54:02.872 --> 00:54:05.666
There's something different
about you, Mr. Laurio.

508
00:54:05.750 --> 00:54:08.669
Yeah. I was having
a good day.

509
00:54:08.753 --> 00:54:12.422
No. No, it's not that.

510
00:54:14.342 --> 00:54:16.760
- Sit down.
- No.

511
00:54:16.844 --> 00:54:19.012
Sit your ass down.

512
00:54:19.097 --> 00:54:22.474
What could it be?

513
00:54:22.558 --> 00:54:25.435
What are you doing?

514
00:54:26.437 --> 00:54:29.439
Ahh. There it is.

515
00:54:30.775 --> 00:54:33.777
Too much iron in your blood.

516
00:54:53.131 --> 00:54:55.674
Mr. Laurio, never trust
a beautiful woman ...

517
00:54:55.758 --> 00:54:58.927
especially one
who's interested in you.

518
00:55:46.267 --> 00:55:48.351
So, uh ...

519
00:55:48.436 --> 00:55:50.937
when did you first know
you were a --

520
00:55:52.774 --> 00:55:54.691
A --
A mutant?

521
00:55:56.110 --> 00:55:58.153
Would you cut that out?

522
00:55:58.279 --> 00:56:00.238
You have to understand,

523
00:56:00.323 --> 00:56:02.574
We thought Bobby
was going to a school
for the gifted.

524
00:56:02.658 --> 00:56:05.952
- Bobby is gifted.
- We know that. We just
didn't realize he was-

525
00:56:06.037 --> 00:56:10.832
We still love you, Bobby.
It's just this mutant problem
is a little --

526
00:56:10.917 --> 00:56:15.670
- What mutant problem?
- Complicated.

527
00:56:15.755 --> 00:56:18.882
What exactly are
you a professor of,
Mr. Logan?

528
00:56:18.966 --> 00:56:21.760
Art.

529
00:56:21.844 --> 00:56:24.095
Well, you should see
what Bobby can do.

530
00:56:30.394 --> 00:56:33.104
Bobby.

531
00:56:36.734 --> 00:56:39.319
I can do a lot more than that.

532
00:56:44.116 --> 00:56:46.451
Oh. Ronny!

533
00:56:50.540 --> 00:56:53.208
This is all my fault.
- Actually ...

534
00:56:53.292 --> 00:56:56.586
they discovered that males
are the ones who carry
the mutant gene and pass it on ...

535
00:56:56.671 --> 00:56:58.463
so it's his fault.

536
00:56:58.548 --> 00:57:00.465
... the assassination attempt ...

537
00:57:03.386 --> 00:57:05.637
911. 
Please state your emergency.

538
00:57:05.721 --> 00:57:08.098
I need the police.
There are people
in our house.

539
00:57:08.224 --> 00:57:10.308
They won't let us leave.
- Authorities refused to comment ...

540
00:57:10.393 --> 00:57:13.186
but it's believed
that a manhunt for several
fugitives from the facility ...

541
00:57:13.271 --> 00:57:15.272
is now underway.

542
00:57:17.817 --> 00:57:21.695
Nobody's responding.
I can't get a signal.

543
00:57:21.779 --> 00:57:23.780
Why don't you take a break?
I'll keep trying.

544
00:57:23.865 --> 00:57:25.866
Right.

545
00:57:54.854 --> 00:57:58.607
So, what are they?

546
00:57:58.691 --> 00:58:01.484
They are angelic symbols ...

547
00:58:01.569 --> 00:58:05.572
passed on to mankind
by the Archangel Gabriel.

548
00:58:05.656 --> 00:58:11.328
They're beautiful.
How many do you have?

549
00:58:11.412 --> 00:58:14.205
One for every sin ...

550
00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:15.790
so quite a few.

551
00:58:19.837 --> 00:58:21.838
You and Miss Grey
are schoolteachers?

552
00:58:21.923 --> 00:58:27.260
Yes. At a school
for people like us ...
where we can be safe.

553
00:58:27.345 --> 00:58:29.512
Safe from what?

554
00:58:29.597 --> 00:58:31.681
Everyone else.

555
00:58:34.143 --> 00:58:38.730
You know, outside of the circus,
most people were afraid of me.

556
00:58:38.814 --> 00:58:42.651
But I didn't hate them.
I pitied them.

557
00:58:43.653 --> 00:58:46.071
Do you know why?

558
00:58:46.155 --> 00:58:49.282
Because most people
will never know anything ...

559
00:58:49.367 --> 00:58:53.370
beyond what they see
with their own two eyes.

560
00:58:53.454 --> 00:58:57.207
Well, I gave up on pity
a long time ago.

561
00:59:01.462 --> 00:59:06.466
Someone so beautiful
should not be so angry.

562
00:59:08.886 --> 00:59:10.804
Sometimes anger ...

563
00:59:10.888 --> 00:59:13.056
can help you survive.

564
00:59:14.976 --> 00:59:16.977
So can faith.

565
00:59:17.061 --> 00:59:20.313
Storm, I found
an active com device.

566
00:59:20.398 --> 00:59:22.190
Where?

567
00:59:30.408 --> 00:59:33.410
Oh, it's for me.

568
00:59:35.579 --> 00:59:37.956
Bobby ...

569
00:59:38.040 --> 00:59:43.128
have you tried
not being a mutant?

570
00:59:43.212 --> 00:59:46.715
No one's left, Jean.
Soldiers came.

571
00:59:46.841 --> 00:59:50.635
What about the children?
Some of them escaped.
I'm not sure about the rest.

572
00:59:50.720 --> 00:59:53.471
We haven't been able
to reach the professor
or Scott either.

573
00:59:53.597 --> 00:59:57.267
Where are you, Logan?
Boston, with
Bobby Drake's family.

574
00:59:57.351 --> 01:00:02.022
- Okay. We're on our way.
- And Storm? Make it fast.

575
01:00:08.362 --> 01:00:09.779
We have to go now.
Why?

576
01:00:09.905 --> 01:00:11.448
Now!
Logan, what's wrong?

577
01:00:16.037 --> 01:00:19.330
Drop the knives
and put your hands in the air.

578
01:00:19.415 --> 01:00:22.625
- What's going on here?
- Ronny.

579
01:00:22.710 --> 01:00:25.295
I said drop the knives.

580
01:00:25.379 --> 01:00:28.673
Open the door!
- Break it.

581
01:00:28.758 --> 01:00:31.051
Turn around.

582
01:00:31.135 --> 01:00:32.469
- Up against the wall.
- Okay!

583
01:00:32.595 --> 01:00:37.682
This is just
a misunderstanding.
Put the knives down.

584
01:00:37.767 --> 01:00:40.226
I can't.

585
01:00:40.311 --> 01:00:42.812
Look.

586
01:00:42.897 --> 01:00:44.314
Oh!

587
01:00:46.025 --> 01:00:50.862
All right, the rest of you,
on the ground now.

588
01:00:50.946 --> 01:00:53.656
Look, kid,
I said on the ground.

589
01:00:59.747 --> 01:01:03.500
We don't want to
hurt you, kid.

590
01:01:07.004 --> 01:01:11.299
You know
all those dangerous mutants
you hear about on the news?

591
01:01:13.469 --> 01:01:15.345
I'm the worst one.

592
01:01:40.621 --> 01:01:42.705
Look out!

593
01:03:21.222 --> 01:03:23.765
Guten Tag.

594
01:03:26.018 --> 01:03:28.228
Who the hell is this?
Kurt Wagner.

595
01:03:28.312 --> 01:03:31.564
But in the Munich circus,
I was known as
"the Incredible Nightcrawler" --

596
01:03:31.649 --> 01:03:34.734
- Aw, save it. Storm?
- We're outta here.

597
01:03:34.860 --> 01:03:37.278
Whoa.

598
01:03:55.714 --> 01:03:58.216
Jason, stop it!

599
01:04:18.904 --> 01:04:23.116
It's all right.

600
01:04:23.242 --> 01:04:25.451
You can come out.
Have they gone?

601
01:04:25.536 --> 01:04:28.121
Yes.

602
01:04:30.165 --> 01:04:34.210
- Where are all the other students?
- I don't know.

603
01:04:34.295 --> 01:04:36.713
Well, then, we'll have to
find them, won't we?

604
01:04:42.720 --> 01:04:46.222
We'll use Cerebro.

605
01:04:46.307 --> 01:04:48.808
Come on.

606
01:04:58.319 --> 01:05:00.987
How far are we?

607
01:05:01.071 --> 01:05:03.573
We're actually coming up
on the mansion now.

608
01:05:05.159 --> 01:05:07.785
I've got two signals approaching.

609
01:05:09.621 --> 01:05:11.539
Coming in fast.

610
01:05:15.961 --> 01:05:20.173
Unidentified aircraft, you are 
ordered to descend to 20,000 feet.

611
01:05:20.257 --> 01:05:24.719
Return with our escort
to Hanscom Air Force base.
You have 10 seconds to comply.

612
01:05:24.803 --> 01:05:27.722
- Wow. Somebody's angry.
- I wonder why.

613
01:05:27.806 --> 01:05:32.352
We are coming up alongside you to 
escort you to Hanscom Air Force base.

614
01:05:32.436 --> 01:05:35.438
Lower your altitude now.

615
01:05:37.816 --> 01:05:41.903
Repeat, lower your altitude to 20,000 feet.
This is your last warning.

616
01:05:46.825 --> 01:05:49.202
They're falling back.

617
01:05:50.996 --> 01:05:52.580
They're marking us.

618
01:05:52.664 --> 01:05:54.457
- What?
- They're gonna fire. Hang on!

619
01:06:05.511 --> 01:06:07.095
I gotta shake 'em.

620
01:06:13.977 --> 01:06:16.479
- Please don't do that again.
- I agree.

621
01:06:19.108 --> 01:06:21.526
Don't we have
any weapons in this heap?

622
01:06:44.133 --> 01:06:46.008
Warning, warning, warning.

623
01:07:03.277 --> 01:07:06.195
Warning, warning, warning,
warning, warning.

624
01:07:09.908 --> 01:07:12.910
Warning, warning, warning,
warning, warning, warning.

625
01:07:12.995 --> 01:07:15.204
Warning, warning, warning --

626
01:07:28.218 --> 01:07:31.637
- Everybody okay back there?
- No.

627
01:07:39.188 --> 01:07:40.730
Oh, my God.
There's two of 'em.

628
01:07:59.958 --> 01:08:02.752
There's one more.

629
01:08:02.836 --> 01:08:04.420
Jean --

630
01:08:05.422 --> 01:08:07.715
Oh, God!

631
01:08:18.769 --> 01:08:22.104
No!

632
01:09:01.520 --> 01:09:04.814
- Jean?
- It's not me.

633
01:09:17.995 --> 01:09:20.871
When will these people
learn how to fly?

634
01:09:38.515 --> 01:09:41.976
Thank you.
Bitte schön.

635
01:09:48.191 --> 01:09:52.903
- Can you hear
what they're saying?
- I could take a closer look.

636
01:09:52.988 --> 01:09:56.032
His name is
Colonel William Stryker ...

637
01:09:56.116 --> 01:09:58.701
and he invaded your mansion
for one purpose:

638
01:09:58.785 --> 01:10:02.330
He wanted Cerebro.

639
01:10:02.414 --> 01:10:04.957
Or enough of it
to build one of his own.

640
01:10:05.042 --> 01:10:10.338
But that doesn't make any sense.
Stryker would need the professor to operate it.

641
01:10:10.422 --> 01:10:13.299
Which I think is the only reason
my old friend is still alive.

642
01:10:13.383 --> 01:10:16.177
Oh, my God.

643
01:10:16.261 --> 01:10:18.971
Now, what are you all so afraid of?

644
01:10:19.056 --> 01:10:21.390
While Cerebro is working,
Charles' mind is connected ...

645
01:10:21.475 --> 01:10:23.643
to every living person
on the planet.

646
01:10:23.727 --> 01:10:26.395
If he were forced to
concentrate hard enough
on a particular group --

647
01:10:26.480 --> 01:10:29.440
let's say, mutants,
for example --

648
01:10:29.524 --> 01:10:32.902
- he could kill us all.
- Wait a minute.

649
01:10:32.986 --> 01:10:36.697
How would Stryker even know
where to find Cerebro
in the first place?

650
01:10:39.910 --> 01:10:41.994
Because I told him.

651
01:10:42.079 --> 01:10:46.457
I helped Charles build it,
remember?

652
01:10:46.541 --> 01:10:50.836
Mr. Stryker has
powerful methods
of persuasion.

653
01:10:50.921 --> 01:10:53.381
Even against a mutant
as strong as Charles.

654
01:10:53.507 --> 01:10:58.302
So who's this
Stryker anyway?
He's a military scientist.

655
01:10:58.387 --> 01:11:02.431
He spent his whole life
trying to solve
the mutant problem.

656
01:11:02.516 --> 01:11:07.269
If you want
a more intimate perspective,
why don't you ask Wolverine?

657
01:11:07.354 --> 01:11:10.981
You don't remember,
do you?

658
01:11:11.066 --> 01:11:15.194
William Stryker, the only
other man I know who can
manipulate adamantium.

659
01:11:15.278 --> 01:11:19.782
The metal on your bones.
It carries his signature.

660
01:11:21.326 --> 01:11:23.786
- But the professor --
- The professor trusted ...

661
01:11:23.870 --> 01:11:27.456
you were smart enough to
discover this on your own.

662
01:11:27.541 --> 01:11:30.292
He gives you more credit
than I do.

663
01:11:30.377 --> 01:11:35.172
- Why do you need us?
- Mystique has discovered plans
of a base ...

664
01:11:35.257 --> 01:11:38.551
that Stryker's been
operating out of for decades.

665
01:11:38.635 --> 01:11:40.886
We know that's where
he's building the second Cerebro ...

666
01:11:40.971 --> 01:11:44.598
but we don't know
where this base is ...

667
01:11:44.683 --> 01:11:47.101
and I believe
one of you might.

668
01:11:47.185 --> 01:11:52.857
- The professor already tried.
- Once again, you think
it's all about you.

669
01:11:56.153 --> 01:11:58.612
Oh ... hello.

670
01:12:04.035 --> 01:12:08.038
I didn't mean to snoop.
Just try and relax.

671
01:12:22.596 --> 01:12:25.806
I'm sorry.

672
01:12:28.351 --> 01:12:31.645
Strykef's at Alkali Lake.

673
01:12:31.730 --> 01:12:34.774
That's where the professor
sent me. There's nothing left.

674
01:12:34.858 --> 01:12:39.820
There's nothing left
on the surface, Logan.
The base is underground.

675
01:12:54.211 --> 01:12:56.462
Hey.
Hey.

676
01:12:57.464 --> 01:13:00.800
You okay?

677
01:13:00.926 --> 01:13:03.260
Yeah.
You sure?

678
01:13:03.386 --> 01:13:07.640
How we doing?
Not good.

679
01:13:07.724 --> 01:13:10.518
It'll take four or five hours before
I can get it off the ground.

680
01:13:10.602 --> 01:13:13.729
That's not what I meant.

681
01:13:13.855 --> 01:13:18.192
I'm just worried
about Scott.
I'm worried about you.

682
01:13:18.276 --> 01:13:21.237
That was some display
of power up there.

683
01:13:21.363 --> 01:13:25.699
Obviously, it wasn't enough.
Hey, hey.
Come on. All right?

684
01:13:28.703 --> 01:13:30.913
I love him.

685
01:13:33.333 --> 01:13:35.251
Do you?

686
01:13:35.335 --> 01:13:37.837
Girls flirt with
the dangerous guy, Logan ...

687
01:13:37.921 --> 01:13:39.922
they don't take him home.

688
01:13:40.006 --> 01:13:42.716
They marry the good guy.

689
01:13:42.801 --> 01:13:44.760
I could be the good guy.

690
01:13:44.845 --> 01:13:47.596
Logan, the good guy
sticks around.

691
01:13:54.229 --> 01:13:57.690
Jean.
Please. Please.

692
01:13:57.816 --> 01:14:00.651
Don't make me
do this.
Do what?

693
01:14:02.237 --> 01:14:04.238
This.

694
01:14:13.582 --> 01:14:16.208
Excuse me.

695
01:14:16.293 --> 01:14:20.880
They say you can
imitate any body ...
even their voice.

696
01:14:20.964 --> 01:14:24.466
Even their voice.

697
01:14:24.551 --> 01:14:28.262
Then why not
stay in disguise
all the time?

698
01:14:28.346 --> 01:14:32.349
You know,
look like everyone else.

699
01:14:32.434 --> 01:14:35.269
Because
we shouldn't have to.

700
01:15:04.174 --> 01:15:06.133
Look --

701
01:15:30.367 --> 01:15:32.576
No one's ever left a scar
quite like you.

702
01:15:32.661 --> 01:15:34.912
What do you want,
an apology?

703
01:15:34.996 --> 01:15:37.414
You know what I want.

704
01:15:39.334 --> 01:15:42.336
But what do you want?

705
01:15:52.389 --> 01:15:55.724
What do you really want?

706
01:15:56.810 --> 01:15:59.228
I want you to get out.

707
01:16:04.901 --> 01:16:07.236
Jesus.

708
01:16:13.368 --> 01:16:15.744
Why don't we get uniforms?
Yeah, where's ours?

709
01:16:15.829 --> 01:16:19.164
They're on order.
Should arrive in a few years.

710
01:16:26.381 --> 01:16:29.258
We love what you've 
done with your hair.

711
01:16:31.261 --> 01:16:35.889
Hey, hey.
Come on. Let's go.

712
01:16:43.023 --> 01:16:46.066
So, they say
you're the bad guy.

713
01:16:46.151 --> 01:16:49.987
Is that what they say?

714
01:16:52.490 --> 01:16:57.494
That's a dorky-looking
helmet. What's it for?

715
01:16:57.579 --> 01:17:00.372
This dorky-looking helmet
is the only thing
that's gonna protect me ...

716
01:17:00.457 --> 01:17:03.125
from the real bad guys.

717
01:17:07.505 --> 01:17:11.467
- What's your name?
- John.

718
01:17:12.510 --> 01:17:16.013
What's your real name,
John?

719
01:17:21.519 --> 01:17:24.021
Pyro.

720
01:17:24.105 --> 01:17:26.231
Quite a talent
you have there, Pyro.

721
01:17:26.316 --> 01:17:29.276
I can only manipulate
the fire.

722
01:17:29.360 --> 01:17:31.070
I can't create it.

723
01:17:31.154 --> 01:17:34.281
You are a god among insects.

724
01:17:34.365 --> 01:17:36.992
Never let anyone tell you different.

725
01:17:56.930 --> 01:18:01.558
Sir, the machine
has been completed
to all specifications.

726
01:18:01.643 --> 01:18:03.435
Good.

727
01:18:03.561 --> 01:18:06.897
Ow!

728
01:18:06.981 --> 01:18:10.901
If I may ask, sir, why are we
keeping the children here?

729
01:18:10.985 --> 01:18:13.695
I'm a scientist,
Sergeant Lyman.

730
01:18:13.780 --> 01:18:18.867
When I build a machine,
I wanna make sure that
it's working.

731
01:18:25.166 --> 01:18:27.459
All right, this is
a topographic map
of the dam.

732
01:18:27.544 --> 01:18:29.461
This is the spillway.

733
01:18:29.546 --> 01:18:32.714
You see these
density changes
in the terrain?

734
01:18:32.841 --> 01:18:34.758
They're tire tracks.
That's the entrance.

735
01:18:34.843 --> 01:18:38.804
Mm-hmm. And this
shows the depth of the ice
that's covering the ground.

736
01:18:38.888 --> 01:18:41.390
Now, this is recent
water activity.

737
01:18:41.474 --> 01:18:43.517
If we go in there,
Stryker could flood
the spillway.

738
01:18:43.601 --> 01:18:45.477
Can you teleport inside?

739
01:18:45.562 --> 01:18:49.690
No. I have to be able
to see where I'm going ...

740
01:18:49.774 --> 01:18:52.526
otherwise I could
wind up inside a wall.

741
01:18:52.610 --> 01:18:56.947
I'll go. I have a hunch
he'll want me alive.

742
01:18:57.031 --> 01:19:01.827
Wolverine, whoever goes into
the dam needs to be able to
operate the spillway mechanism.

743
01:19:01.911 --> 01:19:03.871
What do you intend to do?

744
01:19:03.955 --> 01:19:06.790
Scratch it with your claws?

745
01:19:06.875 --> 01:19:09.168
I'll take my chances.

746
01:19:09.252 --> 01:19:11.753
But I won't.

747
01:19:32.442 --> 01:19:36.778
Sir, there's someone
coming down the spillway.

748
01:19:40.783 --> 01:19:42.951
I'm flooding it.
Wait.

749
01:19:48.625 --> 01:19:51.126
Stryker!

750
01:19:59.385 --> 01:20:01.261
Stryker!

751
01:20:02.305 --> 01:20:06.475
Well, look who's come home.

752
01:20:19.113 --> 01:20:21.823
Move and you're dead.

753
01:20:52.814 --> 01:20:55.065
The one thing I know
better than anyone
is my own work.

754
01:20:55.149 --> 01:20:58.068
Seal the room. Shoot it.

755
01:20:58.152 --> 01:20:59.861
Seal the room
Step away!

756
01:21:15.128 --> 01:21:18.630
We have a metamorph loose.
Could be anybody.

757
01:21:18.715 --> 01:21:20.841
Anybody?
What --

758
01:21:31.394 --> 01:21:33.312
Can you override
the spillway mechanism?

759
01:21:33.396 --> 01:21:36.106
Everything's controlled
from inside that room.
That's why the doors are so thick.

760
01:21:36.190 --> 01:21:39.568
Oh, really?
Get some charges!
Blow the doors open!

761
01:21:41.237 --> 01:21:43.447
Take out these cameras!

762
01:21:47.285 --> 01:21:49.244
I'm in.

763
01:21:49.370 --> 01:21:52.914
She's good.
You have no idea.

764
01:22:04.844 --> 01:22:08.638
Fire in the hole.

765
01:22:12.685 --> 01:22:14.936
Move, move, move.

766
01:22:31.788 --> 01:22:33.955
Sergeant, she's opened
the spillway doors.

767
01:22:34.082 --> 01:22:36.291
More mutants
have entered the base.
How many?

768
01:22:36.376 --> 01:22:38.919
We've lost coms.
There's some sort of
electrical interference --

769
01:22:39.003 --> 01:22:42.547
Sergeant Lyman,
gather the rest of your men
and meet me outside Cerebro.

770
01:22:42.632 --> 01:22:45.842
You carry on.
When I come back, I want
this door open all the way!

771
01:22:59.482 --> 01:23:02.776
Welcome, Professor.

772
01:23:02.860 --> 01:23:07.322
- Don't leave me alone, please?
- You can come inside.

773
01:24:02.128 --> 01:24:03.837
Have you found it?

774
01:24:03.921 --> 01:24:08.383
A large portion of energy
from the dam has been diverted
to this chamber.

775
01:24:08.509 --> 01:24:10.051
- Cerebro.
- There it is.

776
01:24:10.178 --> 01:24:13.388
Can you shut it down
from here?
No.

777
01:24:13.514 --> 01:24:15.724
Come. There's
little time.
Not without us.

778
01:24:19.729 --> 01:24:22.689
Oh, my God.
The children.

779
01:24:22.773 --> 01:24:24.858
- Kurt, will you come with me?
- Yes

780
01:24:24.984 --> 01:24:28.403
- Where are they?
- They're being held in a 
containment cell one level down.

781
01:24:28.488 --> 01:24:31.907
Stryker.
All right ...

782
01:24:31.991 --> 01:24:33.867
we'll get the children
and meet you at Cerebro.

783
01:24:33.951 --> 01:24:38.163
Okay. I'll try to find Scott
and the professor.

784
01:24:38.247 --> 01:24:42.334
- Will you be all right without us?
- Yeah. I'll be fine.

785
01:24:42.418 --> 01:24:44.753
Where's Logan?

786
01:24:50.635 --> 01:24:52.928
He's gone.

787
01:24:54.138 --> 01:24:56.973
You, set up a perimeter.
- Move, move.

788
01:25:36.973 --> 01:25:39.307
Jason.

789
01:25:45.398 --> 01:25:47.482
It's time.

790
01:25:52.530 --> 01:25:54.864
Time to
find our friends.

791
01:26:00.663 --> 01:26:03.331
Is it time to
find our friends?

792
01:26:03.416 --> 01:26:06.626
- All of them.
- All of them?

793
01:26:06.711 --> 01:26:09.337
- All of the mutants.
- All the mutants?

794
01:26:09.422 --> 01:26:13.717
- Everywhere.
- Everywhere?

795
01:26:13.843 --> 01:26:16.595
That's right.
- Every one of them?

796
01:26:16.721 --> 01:26:19.055
Oh, yes.
- Good.

797
01:26:20.057 --> 01:26:24.019
It's time to bring it to an end.

798
01:26:26.105 --> 01:26:28.356
Make me proud.

799
01:26:56.594 --> 01:26:59.721
Just don't move.

800
01:27:01.557 --> 01:27:05.935
Kill anyone who approaches ...
even if it's me.

801
01:27:31.379 --> 01:27:34.297
Go! I'll take care of him!

802
01:27:34.382 --> 01:27:38.093
This is one lover's quarrel we 
cannot get involved in, my dear.

803
01:27:47.144 --> 01:27:50.146
Scott!

804
01:27:50.231 --> 01:27:51.648
Scott?

805
01:27:53.442 --> 01:27:56.945
- Help us! Anybody!
- Listen.

806
01:27:57.029 --> 01:27:59.114
Help! Get us out of here.

807
01:27:59.198 --> 01:28:01.116
- Julie?
- Storm.

808
01:28:01.242 --> 01:28:04.369
Get us out of here!
Okay, we're coming.

809
01:28:17.883 --> 01:28:19.884
Scott!

810
01:28:39.905 --> 01:28:41.865
Scott, don't do this!

811
01:29:34.084 --> 01:29:36.169
Jean, no, no, no.
It's okay.

812
01:29:36.253 --> 01:29:37.754
It's okay. It's me.

813
01:29:37.880 --> 01:29:40.173
Scott.
I'm so sorry.

814
01:29:41.509 --> 01:29:44.511
I thought I'd lost you.
Oh, God.

815
01:29:46.889 --> 01:29:49.599
I'm so sorry. I could see you,
but I couldn't stop myself.

816
01:29:49.725 --> 01:29:51.643
I tried.
I'm sorry.
I love you so much.

817
01:29:51.727 --> 01:29:53.603
I love you.

818
01:29:55.272 --> 01:29:59.025
My leg.
Okay, easy. Easy.

819
01:29:59.109 --> 01:30:00.568
Scott ...

820
01:30:02.905 --> 01:30:05.073
something's wrong.

821
01:30:13.874 --> 01:30:18.378
My God. No!

822
01:30:20.256 --> 01:30:25.343
Have you found the mutants yet?
Have you found all of them?

823
01:30:25.427 --> 01:30:27.929
I'm trying.
There are so many of them.

824
01:30:28.013 --> 01:30:30.723
Then concentrate.

825
01:30:30.808 --> 01:30:32.767
Concentrate.

826
01:32:37.559 --> 01:32:40.979
The tricky thing about
adamantium is ...

827
01:32:41.063 --> 01:32:43.564
that if you ever
manage to process ...

828
01:32:43.649 --> 01:32:48.861
its raw, liquid form,
you gotta keep it that way.

829
01:32:49.863 --> 01:32:53.992
Keep it hot.

830
01:32:54.076 --> 01:32:57.286
Because once the metal cools,
it's indestructible.

831
01:33:00.416 --> 01:33:02.291
But you already
know that.

832
01:33:03.711 --> 01:33:06.421
I used to think you were
one of a kind, Wolverine.

833
01:33:11.218 --> 01:33:13.594
I was wrong.

834
01:33:32.156 --> 01:33:34.365
Holy shit.

835
01:35:18.512 --> 01:35:20.429
That's it.

836
01:35:22.349 --> 01:35:24.267
Whoa. Where do you
think you're going?

837
01:35:24.351 --> 01:35:26.644
I'm sick of this kid's table shit.
I'm going in there.

838
01:35:26.728 --> 01:35:29.689
John, they told us to stay here.

839
01:35:29.773 --> 01:35:31.732
You always do as you're told?

840
01:36:32.920 --> 01:36:35.755
Find all the mutants.

841
01:36:35.839 --> 01:36:37.757
Find them.

842
01:36:37.841 --> 01:36:42.303
Find all the mutants.
Find them all. Each one.
All of them.

843
01:36:42.429 --> 01:36:44.430
Good.
- Kill them.

844
01:37:33.772 --> 01:37:36.148
Concentrate. 
Concentrate harder.

845
01:37:36.233 --> 01:37:38.484
Now, find them all.
Find all the mutants.

846
01:37:38.568 --> 01:37:40.903
You, concentrate harder.

847
01:37:41.947 --> 01:37:46.450
Kill them.
Kill them all.

848
01:37:46.535 --> 01:37:48.452
Kill them.

849
01:37:48.537 --> 01:37:52.498
Cerebro.

850
01:37:52.582 --> 01:37:55.584
We're too late.

851
01:38:04.011 --> 01:38:06.679
Eric, hurry!

852
01:38:53.602 --> 01:38:57.605
That's strange.

853
01:39:34.351 --> 01:39:37.019
How does it look 
from there, Charles?

854
01:39:37.104 --> 01:39:39.271
Still fighting the good fight?

855
01:39:39.356 --> 01:39:43.859
From here, it doesn't
look like they're playing
by your rules.

856
01:39:45.529 --> 01:39:48.614
Maybe it's time to play by theirs.

857
01:40:25.444 --> 01:40:28.904
There's been
a change of plan.

858
01:40:46.756 --> 01:40:50.092
Good-bye, Charles.

859
01:41:05.192 --> 01:41:07.818
There's been
a change of plans.

860
01:41:07.903 --> 01:41:11.489
Now find them.
Find them all --
the humans.

861
01:41:11.573 --> 01:41:13.908
Find all the humans.
Every one.

862
01:41:34.012 --> 01:41:36.430
How does it feel, bub?

863
01:41:40.435 --> 01:41:44.230
Why did you come back?
You cut me open.
You took my life!

864
01:41:44.314 --> 01:41:47.483
You make it sound as if
I stole something from you.

865
01:41:47.567 --> 01:41:51.153
As I recall,
it was you who volunteered
for the procedure.

866
01:41:52.781 --> 01:41:55.950
Who am I?
You ...

867
01:41:56.034 --> 01:41:58.619
are just a failed experiment.

868
01:42:01.915 --> 01:42:03.916
If you really knew
about your past ...

869
01:42:04.000 --> 01:42:06.627
what kind of person you were ...

870
01:42:06.711 --> 01:42:09.255
the work we did together --

871
01:42:09.339 --> 01:42:13.342
People don't change,
Wolverine.

872
01:42:13.426 --> 01:42:16.136
You were an animal then.
You're an animal now.

873
01:42:16.221 --> 01:42:18.597
I just gave you claws.

874
01:42:42.706 --> 01:42:46.083
What the hell is that?
What is it?

875
01:42:46.167 --> 01:42:50.212
The dam's ruptured.
It's gonna flood water
into the spillway.

876
01:42:50.297 --> 01:42:54.800
It's trying to relieve the pressure.
It's too late.

877
01:42:54.884 --> 01:42:57.261
In a few minutes,
we'll all be underwater.

878
01:42:57.345 --> 01:43:00.264
Come with me, and I'll tell you
everything you want to know.

879
01:43:00.348 --> 01:43:04.435
You can't help your friends.
They're as good as dead,
Wolverine.

880
01:43:04.519 --> 01:43:09.398
You're a survivor,
always have been.

881
01:43:09.482 --> 01:43:13.819
Oh, I thought
I was just an animal ...
with claws.

882
01:43:17.365 --> 01:43:19.825
If we die, you die.

883
01:43:26.041 --> 01:43:28.584
Aaah!

884
01:43:28.668 --> 01:43:31.503
There are no answers that way, Wolverine!

885
01:43:31.588 --> 01:43:36.508
Find all the humans.
Every one. Find them.

886
01:43:36.593 --> 01:43:39.094
Find all the humans.
Find them all.

887
01:43:41.640 --> 01:43:45.225
- What is this?
- Cerebro.

888
01:43:47.103 --> 01:43:48.729
Storm.

889
01:43:48.855 --> 01:43:51.523
Jean.
Are you okay?
Yeah. I'm fine.

890
01:43:51.608 --> 01:43:53.817
What's happening?

891
01:43:53.902 --> 01:43:57.154
Professor's still in there ...
with another mutant.

892
01:43:57.238 --> 01:44:00.491
He's trapped
in some kind of illusion.

893
01:44:00.575 --> 01:44:03.118
Oh, my God.

894
01:44:03.203 --> 01:44:06.163
Magneto's reversed Cerebro.
It's not targeting mutants anymore.

895
01:44:06.247 --> 01:44:10.125
- Who is it targeting?
- Everyone else.

896
01:44:26.935 --> 01:44:29.603
Impossible.

897
01:44:56.131 --> 01:44:59.341
- Everybody stand back.
- Scott, no. His mind is connected 
to Cerebro.

898
01:44:59.426 --> 01:45:03.178
Opening the door could kill him
and everyone his mind is linked to.

899
01:45:03.263 --> 01:45:06.765
Wait. Kurt,
I need you to
take me inside.

900
01:45:06.850 --> 01:45:09.727
- Storm, who is this guy?
Who are you?
- My name is Kurt Wagner ...

901
01:45:09.853 --> 01:45:13.814
but in the Munich circus --
He's a teleporter.

902
01:45:13.898 --> 01:45:16.984
I told you, if I can't see
where I'm going --

903
01:45:17.068 --> 01:45:19.987
I have faith in you.

904
01:45:23.658 --> 01:45:26.201
Don't believe
anything you see in there.

905
01:45:30.665 --> 01:45:34.543
Our Father,
who art in heaven,
hallowed be thy name.

906
01:45:34.627 --> 01:45:37.629
Thy kingdom come,
thy will be done on Earth --

907
01:45:37.756 --> 01:45:42.217
As it is in heaven.

908
01:45:51.811 --> 01:45:53.729
Hello.

909
01:45:55.023 --> 01:45:57.024
What are you looking for?

910
01:45:58.818 --> 01:46:03.405
Professor, can you hear me?

911
01:46:03.490 --> 01:46:07.576
- You've got to stop Cerebro now.
- Who are you talking to?

912
01:46:09.370 --> 01:46:11.121
No. Don't move.

913
01:46:11.206 --> 01:46:13.624
But she's just a little girl.

914
01:46:13.708 --> 01:46:16.001
No, she's not.

915
01:46:19.589 --> 01:46:23.342
I've got my eyes on you.

916
01:46:27.639 --> 01:46:30.140
Mr. Stryker.

917
01:46:30.225 --> 01:46:32.851
Funny, we keep
running into each other.

918
01:46:32.936 --> 01:46:36.980
Mark my words,
it'll never happen again.

919
01:46:40.109 --> 01:46:44.112
Kurt, it's about to 
get very cold in here.

920
01:46:44.197 --> 01:46:47.366
I'm not going anywhere.

921
01:46:53.039 --> 01:46:54.915
What are you doing?

922
01:47:32.287 --> 01:47:34.955
Find all the humans. 
Kill them.

923
01:47:35.039 --> 01:47:37.124
Every single one.
Find all the humans.

924
01:47:39.586 --> 01:47:43.922
Focus. Focus.
Find all the humans.

925
01:47:51.556 --> 01:47:54.600
Stop it!

926
01:48:02.317 --> 01:48:07.571
He's going to be
so angry at me.

927
01:48:35.183 --> 01:48:39.019
Logan. 
Logan, where are you?

928
01:49:09.467 --> 01:49:11.385
We have to get out
through the spillway.

929
01:49:49.507 --> 01:49:52.426
You don't want to go
that way. Trust me.

930
01:50:03.479 --> 01:50:07.107
Come on. There's another 
way out of here.

931
01:50:38.723 --> 01:50:41.141
The helicopter
was right here!

932
01:51:24.310 --> 01:51:28.146
I will take him.
Okay.

933
01:51:53.798 --> 01:51:57.300
It's okay, Rogue. It's okay.
You can let go, honey.

934
01:51:57.385 --> 01:52:00.345
- Let go.
- Go. I'll be fine.

935
01:52:00.471 --> 01:52:03.056
You sure?
Yeah.

936
01:52:14.777 --> 01:52:17.154
Who has the answers,
Wolverine?

937
01:52:17.238 --> 01:52:19.948
Those people?

938
01:52:20.032 --> 01:52:23.535
That creature
in your arms?

939
01:52:25.204 --> 01:52:26.830
Huh?

940
01:52:26.914 --> 01:52:28.874
Huh?

941
01:52:38.092 --> 01:52:40.177
I'll take my chances with him.

942
01:52:43.055 --> 01:52:46.808
One day, someone will finish
what I've started, Wolverine!

943
01:52:46.893 --> 01:52:52.856
One day!

944
01:52:57.111 --> 01:53:01.781
Scott, we've got to
get to Washington.

945
01:53:03.618 --> 01:53:07.787
I fear this has gone beyond Alkali Lake.

946
01:53:08.831 --> 01:53:10.916
Bobby.
I got 'im.

947
01:53:13.044 --> 01:53:15.170
You okay?

948
01:53:15.254 --> 01:53:18.089
I am now.

949
01:53:26.307 --> 01:53:28.266
- What's wrong?
- Vertical thrusters are off line.

950
01:53:28.351 --> 01:53:29.517
So fix 'em.
- I'm trying.

951
01:53:29.602 --> 01:53:32.354
- Has anyone seen John?
- Pyro?

952
01:53:32.438 --> 01:53:34.356
Where the hell
is he?

953
01:53:34.440 --> 01:53:37.025
He's with Magneto.

954
01:53:37.109 --> 01:53:40.278
They're functioning, but I don't 
know how long they're going to last.

955
01:53:40.363 --> 01:53:42.280
I'm trying to override.
It's not responding.

956
01:53:42.365 --> 01:53:47.452
- Come on!
- Oh, no, we've lost the power.

957
01:53:57.088 --> 01:53:59.756
There's power in the fuel cells,
we're just not connecting.

958
01:53:59.840 --> 01:54:01.758
Okay. I've --

959
01:54:19.902 --> 01:54:22.862
Scott, the engine
control system is shot.

960
01:54:22.947 --> 01:54:26.908
- Which part?
- All of it.

961
01:54:29.453 --> 01:54:33.581
- Where's the override?
- It's gonna take some time.

962
01:54:48.431 --> 01:54:50.932
Storm, we need some 
kind of external power.

963
01:54:51.017 --> 01:54:53.560
- Jean?
- Wait. Where is Jean?

964
01:54:55.730 --> 01:54:58.523
She's outside.

965
01:55:12.621 --> 01:55:14.706
No, we're not leaving!
Lower the ramp!

966
01:55:28.763 --> 01:55:30.513
Storm, lower it!

967
01:55:30.598 --> 01:55:32.766
I can't.

968
01:55:54.455 --> 01:55:56.539
She's controlling the jet.

969
01:56:02.463 --> 01:56:06.132
You, get her, now!
She's not letting me.

970
01:56:06.217 --> 01:56:07.467
Damn it!

971
01:56:12.681 --> 01:56:16.810
I know what I'm doing.

972
01:56:16.894 --> 01:56:19.771
- This is --
... the only way.

973
01:56:21.357 --> 01:56:25.527
Jean, listen to me.

974
01:56:27.196 --> 01:56:30.073
Don't do this.
Good-bye.

975
01:56:30.157 --> 01:56:34.828
- Oh, no! No!
- No! No!

976
01:56:59.186 --> 01:57:01.146
She's gone.

977
01:57:03.190 --> 01:57:07.318
- She's gone.
- Don't you say that!

978
01:57:07.445 --> 01:57:08.945
We gotta go back.
She's gone.

979
01:57:09.029 --> 01:57:12.824
No! No.

980
01:57:29.133 --> 01:57:33.136
She's gone.
She's gone. She's --

981
01:57:35.973 --> 01:57:37.891
She's gone.

982
01:57:49.570 --> 01:57:51.988
The Lord is my shepherd.
I shall not want.

983
01:57:52.072 --> 01:57:56.868
He maketh me to lie down
in green pastures.

984
01:57:56.952 --> 01:58:00.830
Yea, though I walk through
the valley of the shadow
of the death ...

985
01:58:00.915 --> 01:58:03.249
I will fear no evil ...

986
01:58:04.919 --> 01:58:08.004
for thou art with me.

987
01:58:19.308 --> 01:58:23.061
Today I've been given
an opportunity to shed light
on recent occurrences ...

988
01:58:23.145 --> 01:58:25.313
from the attack that
ended in this office --
Good morning.

989
01:58:25.397 --> 01:58:27.774
Good morning -- to
the unexplained phenomenon
that swept the Earth ...

990
01:58:27.900 --> 01:58:30.527
nearly annihilating
our way of life.
Good morning, Mr. President.

991
01:58:30.611 --> 01:58:33.863
Good morning. Do we like
this word "annihilating"?

992
01:58:33.948 --> 01:58:36.908
Good morning.

993
01:58:36.992 --> 01:58:40.370
Good morning,
Mr. President.

994
01:58:40.454 --> 01:58:41.746
Thank you.

995
01:58:48.712 --> 01:58:52.465
Mr. President,
we're live in five, four,
three, two-

996
01:58:54.468 --> 01:58:58.888
My fellow Americans,
in this time of adversity ...

997
01:58:58.973 --> 01:59:01.224
we are being offered
a moment ...

998
01:59:01.308 --> 01:59:05.228
a moment
to recognize a growing threat
within our own population ...

999
01:59:05.312 --> 01:59:09.482
and take a unique role
in the shape of human events.

1000
01:59:14.321 --> 01:59:16.990
Did we just lose the feed?
Are we still live?

1001
01:59:52.693 --> 01:59:56.446
Good morning, Mr. President.

1002
01:59:56.530 --> 02:00:00.992
Please, don't be alarmed.
We're not going to harm anyone.

1003
02:00:01.076 --> 02:00:05.121
- Who are you people?
- We're mutants.

1004
02:00:05.205 --> 02:00:08.499
My name is Charles Xavier.
Please, sit down.

1005
02:00:08.584 --> 02:00:13.171
- I'd rather stand.
- Rogue.

1006
02:00:13.255 --> 02:00:17.675
These files were taken
from the private offices
of William Stryker.

1007
02:00:26.769 --> 02:00:28.978
How did you get this?

1008
02:00:29.063 --> 02:00:32.732
Well, let's just say I know a little girl
who can walk through walls.

1009
02:00:42.993 --> 02:00:45.078
I've never seen
this information.
I know.

1010
02:00:45.162 --> 02:00:47.330
Then you also know
I don't respond well to threats.

1011
02:00:47.414 --> 02:00:50.875
Mr. President, this is not a threat.
This is an opportunity.

1012
02:00:50.959 --> 02:00:55.088
There are forces in this world,
both mutant and human alike ...

1013
02:00:55.172 --> 02:00:57.507
who believe that a war is coming.

1014
02:00:57.591 --> 02:01:01.427
You will see from those files
that some have already
tried to start one ...

1015
02:01:01.512 --> 02:01:05.181
and there have been casualties.

1016
02:01:05.265 --> 02:01:07.767
Losses on both sides.

1017
02:01:13.691 --> 02:01:16.859
Mr. President ...

1018
02:01:16.944 --> 02:01:20.738
what you were about to
tell the world is true --
this is a moment.

1019
02:01:20.823 --> 02:01:23.533
A moment to repeat
the mistakes of the past ...

1020
02:01:23.617 --> 02:01:27.453
or to work together
for a better future.

1021
02:01:27.538 --> 02:01:33.209
We're here to stay, Mr. President.
The next move is yours.

1022
02:01:33.293 --> 02:01:36.045
We'll be watching.

1023
02:01:53.772 --> 02:01:57.650
Mr. President.

1024
02:02:24.678 --> 02:02:26.596
You know ...

1025
02:02:26.680 --> 02:02:29.265
even when Jean
was a student ...

1026
02:02:29.349 --> 02:02:32.435
she was always hesitant
about her powers.

1027
02:02:32.519 --> 02:02:37.315
Always looking to others.

1028
02:02:37.399 --> 02:02:42.361
Feeling that in some way
she was left behind.

1029
02:02:46.283 --> 02:02:48.201
Do you think --

1030
02:02:48.285 --> 02:02:52.079
Could we have done
more to save her?

1031
02:02:53.415 --> 02:02:57.543
In the past, she may have let us.

1032
02:02:57.628 --> 02:03:01.214
There had to be another way.

1033
02:03:01.298 --> 02:03:03.800
Why did she leave the plane?

1034
02:03:06.053 --> 02:03:09.972
Because she made a choice.

1035
02:03:10.057 --> 02:03:13.976
Yes, come on in.

1036
02:03:25.531 --> 02:03:27.740
Hey, hey.

1037
02:03:29.701 --> 02:03:33.246
Listen, she did make a choice.

1038
02:03:35.707 --> 02:03:37.708
It was you.

1039
02:04:10.450 --> 02:04:12.952
Professor?

1040
02:04:13.036 --> 02:04:15.079
Is everything all right?

1041
02:04:17.833 --> 02:04:21.043
Yes, I think it will be.

1042
02:04:21.128 --> 02:04:24.088
Now, tell me, have any
of you read a book ...

1043
02:04:24.172 --> 02:04:27.800
by an English novelist
named T.H. White ...

1044
02:04:27.885 --> 02:04:31.178
called: "The Once and Future King?"

1045
02:04:31.263 --> 02:04:33.848
No? Well --

1046
02:04:39.271 --> 02:04:40.813
Mutation.

1047
02:04:40.898 --> 02:04:43.149
It is the key
to our evolution.

1048
02:04:43.233 --> 02:04:46.235
It is how we have evolved from
a single-celled organism ...

1049
02:04:46.320 --> 02:04:49.363
into the dominant species
on the planet.

1050
02:04:49.448 --> 02:04:51.282
This process is slow ...

1051
02:04:51.366 --> 02:04:55.077
normally taking thousands
and thousands of years.

1052
02:04:55.162 --> 02:04:58.122
But every
few hundred millennia ...
